--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Create and setup non-upgradeable objects
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Greengage 7 requires a unique index on a partitioned table to contain every
-- partitioning column. Greengage 6 allows such an index, the initialize data
-- migration scripts drop it and the finalize ones replay its definition, which
-- the target cluster rejects. Nothing can recreate it there, so the upgrade has
-- to stop before anything is dropped.
CREATE SCHEMA unsupported_unique_index;
CREATE SCHEMA
SET search_path TO unsupported_unique_index;
SET

CREATE TABLE sales (trans_id int, office_id int, region text) DISTRIBUTED BY (trans_id) PARTITION BY RANGE (office_id) (START (1) END (4) EVERY (1));
CREATE TABLE
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX sales_unique_idx ON sales(trans_id);
CREATE INDEX

-- a multi level partitioned table is missing the partitioning columns of every level
CREATE TABLE ml_sales (trans_id int, office_id int, region int, dummy int) DISTRIBUTED BY (trans_id) PARTITION BY RANGE (office_id) SUBPARTITION BY RANGE (dummy) SUBPARTITION TEMPLATE (START (1) END (16) EVERY (4)) (START (1) END (3) EVERY (1));
CREATE TABLE
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ml_sales_unique_idx ON ml_sales(trans_id);
CREATE INDEX

RESET search_path;
RESET

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Assert that ggupgrade correctly detects the non-upgradeable objects
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!\retcode ggupgrade initialize --source-gphome="${GPHOME_SOURCE}" --target-gphome=${GPHOME_TARGET} --source-master-port=${PGPORT} --disk-free-ratio 0 --non-interactive;
-- start_ignore

Initialize in progress.

Verifying source and target cluster versions...                    [IN PROGRESS]
Verifying source and target cluster versions...                    [COMPLETE]   
Saving source cluster configuration...                             [IN PROGRESS]
Saving source cluster configuration...                             [COMPLETE]   
Starting ggupgrade hub process...                                  [IN PROGRESS]
Starting ggupgrade hub process...                                  [COMPLETE]   
Checking for plpython2u...                                         [IN PROGRESS]
Checking for plpython2u...                                         [COMPLETE]   
Checking for unique indexes on partitioned tables...               [IN PROGRESS]
Checking for unique indexes on partitioned tables...               [FAILED]     

Error: substep "check_for_unsupported_unique_indexes": Can not start migration because the cluster has unique indexes on partitioned tables that do not contain all of the partitioning columns.

Greengage 7 requires a unique index on a partitioned table to contain every partitioning column:

'''
ERROR:  unique constraint on partitioned table must include all partitioning columns
DETAIL:  UNIQUE constraint on table "sales" lacks column "office_id" which is part of the partition key.
'''

Such an index has to be dropped before the upgrade and cannot be recreated afterwards. Were the
migration to start, the index would be lost and the finalize phase would fail on a cluster that has
already been upgraded.

Affected databases, tables and indexes are listed in this file:
'/home/gpadmin/gpAdminLogs/ggupgrade/partitioned_tables_with_unsupported_unique_indexes.txt'

For each of them either drop the index:

'''
DROP INDEX <schema>.<index>;
'''

or recreate it with the partitioning columns included:

'''
DROP INDEX <schema>.<index>;
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX <index> ON <schema>.<table> (<original columns>, <missing columns>);
'''


NEXT ACTIONS
------------
Please address the above issue and run "ggupgrade initialize" again.
If you would like to return the cluster to its original state, please run "ggupgrade revert".

-- end_ignore
(exited with code 1)
! cat ~/gpAdminLogs/ggupgrade/partitioned_tables_with_unsupported_unique_indexes.txt;
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Database: isolation2test
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
unsupported_unique_index.ml_sales_unique_idx does not contain the partitioning columns office_id, dummy of table unsupported_unique_index.ml_sales
unsupported_unique_index.sales_unique_idx does not contain the partitioning columns office_id of table unsupported_unique_index.sales


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Workaround to unblock upgrade
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DROP SCHEMA unsupported_unique_index CASCADE;
DROP SCHEMA
